Elizabeth smarts father says there is  something he has to talk about 17 years  after his daughter's kidnapping and  miraculous rescue yet smart is revealing  how he struggled to come out as gay his  first Network TV interview about his  sexuality his story was first reported  back in August but this is the first  time that he's talking about it publicly  the 64 year old man who was married to  his former wife Louis for 34 years and  the father of six children told us how  difficult it was to reconcile his faith  with his feelings during the course of  my life you know I've certainly found  you know men to be attractive I was  taught that that was not acceptable that  that was something that you were a  deviant you were a bad person if you  thought those things but you know you're  not a deviant head no no but that was  what I was brought up to believe I never  wanted to identify as being gay I never  wanted that to be part of me mm-hmm why  would God give this to me why would I  have to endure this in life how did you  try to fix it I went to therapists I  went to my church leaders I mean I  literally called my bishop up one  morning and I said you know I feel like  I've stabbed Louis in the heart and I  went to my other church leader and I  said to him so am i gay am i gay and he  said to me I don't think so he said you  know there's this spectrum and it's  fluid within this spectrum when he said  I don't think you're gay did you feel  relieved at hearing that you're thinking  okay maybe I'm not yes I was praying  that I was not I didn't want to believe  that I was  how do you get how do you cure being gay  there is no cure and for all of those  out there that are struggling in this  same spot there is no cure but that's  part of why you're speaking yes it is it  is the reason why I'm speaking this is  absolutely not a choice and I wish my  wife knew that I wish that worth  anything  he is so concerned it is I have to say  very powerful even we all walked out of  there your heart just opens up to him  because can you imagine living your  whole life not being able to be who you  are he's very very concerned about his  ex-wife Louis because the last thing he  wants is hurt her and certainly not hurt  his family but he said he could just no  longer live this way you know people  would say he had you have a problem he  goes you know what my problem was I was  a gay man trying to be straight yeah  that was my problem yeah now you know he  wants to speak out to help others  because he said it really was torturous  for him and imagine what it was like  when Elizabeth Smart disappeared he was  front and center the the public phase he  was worried about that then there was a  lot going on so we will continue our  conversation tomorrow thankful thankful  that he thinks he needs a cure kind of  the guilt the grief and then relief  ultimately he's not the only one from  that generation oh I know I know I  believe that too Tony you'll see more of  our conversation with Edie smart  tomorrow  he'll talk about the difficult process  of coming out to his family
 

